(3) GAP GEOMETRY  A(L) | G(L_G) | B(L) | C(L), G traced out, Petz channel on B.
    Massless Dirac (c=1): the two-interval entropies give exactly
      I(A:C|B) = (1/3) log[(a+g+b)(g+b+c)/((g+b)(a+g+b+c))],
    i.e. the adjacent-interval law with L_B -> L_B + L_G, and the cross ratio
      eta_g = a c/[(a+g+b)(g+b+c)]  ->  a c/L_G^2,  so I ~ L_G^-2, -logF ~ L_G^-4.
